Title: NICK AND ME
Credit: Written by
Author: Author
Source: Adapted from the book
Draft date: 7/30/2026

FADE IN:

INT. PETER'S SEATTLE APARTMENT - DAY

Rain mists against a floor-to-ceiling window overlooking Puget Sound. 

PETER OLSON (30s, lean, neat shirt, composed and quiet) stands by the glass holding a steaming mug. He looks out over the gray water.

PETER (V.O.)
Big brother was mine. Nick was the guy everybody was scared of. He had a pair on him the size of steel wrecking balls, and a face like a puzzle held together with glue. A few scars on his chin and eyebrow. When he walked into a room, people moved out of the way.

EXT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - DAY (FLASHBACK)

A weather-worn five-story brick walk-up in downtown Milwaukee. 

Younger PETER (20, thin, wearing a pizza shop t-shirt) trudges up the concrete steps carrying two grocery bags. 

NICK OLSON (20s, massive, muscular, uncombed reddish-brown hair, scarred left eyebrow) strides past him carrying six heavy shopping bags in one trip like a world's strongest man contestant.

INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - LIVING ROOM - DAY

A cramped, dark apartment filled with old furniture. 

MA (60s, frail, tired brown eyes, worn housecoat) sits in an overstuffed armchair staring blankly at a muted game show.

Nick sets the six bags down on the kitchen counter with a heavy thud.

NICK
What's Ma doin' back in the bedroom at this time of day? You got to keep an eye on her. She shouldn't be sleeping in the middle of the day like that. That's how old people go downhill.

PETER
I know, Nick. I'll make her sit out here.

NICK
It's your responsibility. You're living here to keep an eye on her.

Peter nods silently, looking down at his shoes.

EXT. MILWAUKEE PIZZA PARLOR - DAY

Peter rides his bicycle up to the curb, dismounts, and walks toward the front entrance. 

SIONNA (20s, pale skin, short brown hair, striking light blue eyes, carrying a heavy backpack) trips on an uneven pavement slab and brushes into Peter's shoulder.

PETER
Are you okay?

SIONNA
Yes.

She brushes off her black V-neck shirt and looks up at him. Her eyes catch the daylight.

PETER
I work here. I'm just going to work. What is your name?

SIONNA
Sionna.

PETER
Sionna? That's different. What does that mean?

SIONNA
My mom and dad named me after an Irish goddess. The River Shannon.

PETER
You want to come in and have some pizza?

SIONNA
No thanks, I don't eat pizza. But if you want to go have a cup of coffee sometime, you can call me.

She hands him a small slip of paper with a phone number.

PETER (V.O.)
She spoke like cool blue, like the cool blue of her eyes. No girl had ever been interested in me before. 

INT. JAVA HUT - DAY

A bohemian coffee shop filled with college students, stacks of textbooks, and hanging warmth.

Peter and Sionna sit across from each other at a small wooden table. Sionna turns the pages of a worn paperback copy of Wuthering Heights.

SIONNA
The love that Heathcliff has for Catherine never changes, but in the end that kind of love destroys him. A love that never changes will destroy you.

PETER
Like it consumes you?

SIONNA
We have to be willing to let go of things, and accept things that happen to us, without grasping onto them.

PETER (V.O.)
She made me feel smarter just by being around her. Something inside of me was coming awake. 

INT. JOE'S BAR - NIGHT

A crowded, smoky Milwaukee dive bar. Rock music blares from corner speakers. Neon beer signs glow against wood paneling.

Nick sits at the bar taking a long drag from a tumbler of Jack and Cokes. BOB (20s, unkempt, stoned look) sits beside him. Peter sits on a stool next to them holding a single beer.

Nick turns his head toward the back room where pool tables are lined up. 

LINDSEY (20s, blonde) stands by a cue rack. A DARK-HAIRED MAN in a leather jacket stands beside her, his arm wrapped around her waist.

NICK
Who's she with? Who's that asshole?

PETER
Why does it matter, Bro? You broke up with her. Drop it, man. She can see whoever she wants.

NICK
Kiss my ass. Did I ask your opinion?

Nick slams his tumbler down and strides aggressively into the pool room. Bob and Peter follow behind him.

INT. JOE'S BAR - POOL ROOM - NIGHT

Nick confronts Lindsey and the dark-haired man. Pool players pause their games, leaning on their cues.

DARK-HAIRED MAN
What the fuck is wrong with you? You got a problem with me?

Nick's face turns beet red. His fists clench tightly.

Peter steps directly between Nick and the man, holding his hands up to push Nick back.

PETER
Nick! Nick, listen! You don't have any problem with this guy! Leave it, man, just leave it!

NICK
Keep out of it! It's none of your goddamn business! You're going to be next if you don't get out of my face, asshole!

PETER
Stop it! Stop it! You're crazy as shit! No one cares about your ego, Nick!

Nick's brow creases in pure rage. He draws his right fist back and swings directly at Peter's face. 

Peter flinches back violently, avoiding the blow as JOE THE BAR OWNER and a LARGE BOUNCER rush in to tackle Nick. 

Chairs scrape, shouting erupts. Peter turns and bolts for the exit door.

EXT. MILWAUKEE STREET - NIGHT

Peter runs through the freezing night air, lungs burning, feet pounding the sidewalk until he reaches a quiet street.

INT. SIONNA'S DUPLEX - LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Peter sits on a green suede couch, head buried in his hands. Sionna sits beside him, gently stroking his hair.

SIONNA
Your brother tried to hit you.

PETER
Yes, he did.

SIONNA
He is a controlling ass, and you are showing him that you don't need him. You are becoming a bravely compassionate being. You can't let him intimidate you.

PETER
What is my purpose?

SIONNA
The purpose of your life is to find the true self within you, and to honor it.

INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Nick stands over Peter near the hallway, towering over him, eyes dark with fury. Ma sits in her chair, shaking her head side to side silently.

NICK
You're some hot shit college kid now with a hoity-toity girlfriend, and you know everything!

PETER
Nick, I'm not like that! I'm just working my ass off and taking classes. I need my family to support me on this!

NICK
Don't you ever, EVER interrupt me in public again. You got that?

PETER
I got it, Nick.

Nick grabs Peter's shirt collar, pulling Peter's face inches from his own.

NICK
You take care of Ma.

Nick lets go, turns on his heel, and slams the apartment door so hard the framed prints rattle on the wall.

INT. KIRK STREET APARTMENT - LIVING ROOM - DAY

Morning light filters through dusty blinds. 

Peter enters from the hallway, dressed in his pizza delivery shirt. The apartment is dead silent.

PETER
Ma?

The room is empty. Ma's purse and coat are gone. 

On the kitchen counter, the answering machine light blinks rapidly. Peter presses the button.

OFFICER DUPUIS (V.O.)
Mr. Olson, this is Officer Dupuis from the Milwaukee County Sheriff's Department. We need to talk to you regarding an accident involving your brother Nicholas and your mother Olivia.

INT. HOSPITAL ICU ROOM - DAY

Flashing medical monitors beep rhythmically. 

OFFICER DUPUIS (50s, graying hair, mustache) stands beside Peter in the sterile corridor outside an ICU room.

OFFICER DUPUIS
Last night about 8 p.m. they were hit broadside at Werner and Lowe. Your mother passed away at the scene. Your brother is in serious condition. Toxicology is pending—we believe he was driving under the influence.

Peter stares through the glass window of the ICU room. 

Inside, Nick lies unconscious in a hospital bed, face bruised green and purple, legs in traction, tubes running into his nose and chest.

Peter steps into the room, approaching the foot of the bed. Nick slowly blinks his bloodshot eyes open.

NICK
(weakly)
Hey, Bro... I guess I really fucked up, man... Can't believe Ma's gone...

PETER
The mass was nice. She's at peace now.

NICK
The cops are after me... They're saying vehicular manslaughter. Like it was all my fault!

PETER
Whose fault was it, Nick?

NICK
What do you mean? You think I meant to kill her? You son of a bitch!

PETER
Think about it, Nick.

Peter turns around and walks out of the room, leaving Nick trapped in the hospital bed.

INT. SIONNA'S DUPLEX - LIVING ROOM - NIGHT

Rain lashes against the living room window. Sionna sits alone in a brown armchair reading notes under a floor lamp. 

A loud, heavy KNOCK rattles the front door. 

Sionna opens the door a crack. 

Nick stands on the porch in a heavy coat, pale, bruised, limping heavily on a cane, eyes wild and bloodshot.

SIONNA
Nick? Is that you?

Nick shoves the door open with his shoulder, stepping inside.

NICK
You're the reason I'm probably going to jail. You know that?

SIONNA
Let's talk about this rationally—

NICK
No! If it wasn't for you messing around with my brother, everything would be cool! He would be taking care of Ma! She'd be alive!

Nick corners Sionna against the hallway wall, dropping his cane. He grabs her throat with his left hand, pressing her hard against the plaster.

SIONNA
(choking)
Nick—stop—

Nick reaches into his coat pocket with his right hand and flicks open a sharp SWISS ARMY KNIFE blade. He holds the steel edge against her chest.

NICK
Break it off with him tonight or else. I'll be back in one week and if you leak one word to the cops, my friends will find your parents.

The front door BURSTS open. Peter rushes into the hallway.

PETER
Holy shit, Nick! What the fuck are you doing?!

Peter grabs Nick's coat sleeve to pull him away. 

Nick thrusts his elbow backward into Peter's face. In the chaos, Nick lunges forward with the blade.

The knife drives deep into Sionna's shoulder. Blood spatters against her light shirt. She collapses onto the floorboards with a gasp.

Nick stares at the blood on his hands, turns, and flees out the open front door into the rain.

Peter drops to his knees beside Sionna, pressing both hands flat over the bleeding wound.

PETER
Sionna! Sionna, stay with me!

He reaches frantically with one bloodied hand for the telephone on the end table, dialing 911.

PETER (CONT'D)
(into phone, sobbing)
I need an ambulance! Please, hurry!

INT. SIONNA'S DUPLEX - LIVING ROOM - DAY (MONTHS LATER)

Winter sunlight reflects off snow outside. 

Sionna sits in a rocking chair, her left arm supported in a sling. Her face is pale, her blue eyes dark and hollow.

Peter sits on the edge of the couch across from her.

PETER
Sionna? Please talk to me. 

SIONNA
(whispering)
I can't feel myself anymore. 

PETER
I love you. You're safe now. He's going to prison.

SIONNA
(staring at her hands)
As long as there is any doubt, I can't go on with you. I need to go to my parents' farm.

Peter looks down, tears falling onto his hands. Sionna slowly gets up and walks down the dark hallway toward her bedroom.

PETER (V.O.)
Siona was my life guide. She had awoken me from a monotonous life. And now she was gone.

INT. GREEN BAY CORRECTIONAL - VISITATION ROOM - DAY (YEARS LATER)

A stark, sterile visitation room divided by thick glass partition walls. 

Peter (now 30s, dressed in a sharp blazer, clean-cut and confident) sits at a counter holding a yellow telephone receiver.

On the other side of the glass sits Nick (gaunt, graying hair, wearing a bright orange prison jumpsuit). 

NICK
(through phone)
Hi, Bro. Glad you came.

PETER
I'm here to tell you some things, Nick. And I want you to listen to me. I have spent the last eight years thinking and growing. I've come to realize a few things about you. You're an asshole. You're an asshole that killed my mother. And you're an asshole for trying to kill Sionna.

Nick stares down at the counter in silence.

PETER (CONT'D)
Now that you know how I feel, I have to add this bit. I forgive you. I forgive you, Nick, because it sets me free. It releases your control over me forever.

Tears well up in Nick's eyes, spilling down his cheeks onto the glass counter.

NICK
I'm so sorry... You're right, man... I am a huge asshole. You're a big man, and I'm a small one.

A CORRECTIONAL OFFICER taps Nick on the shoulder.

CORRECTIONAL OFFICER
Time's up, Olson.

NICK
What are you doing now, Peter?

PETER
I own a pizza chain in Seattle. We're expanding. 

NICK
(smiling through tears)
President Olson. That's amazing, man. I'm proud of you.

Peter hangs up the receiver. 

Nick is led away down the concrete corridor by the guard. Peter stands up, smooths his jacket, and walks toward the exit doors.

INT. PETER'S SEATTLE APARTMENT - DAY (RETURN TO FRAME)

Peter stands by the floor-to-ceiling window in his Seattle apartment, looking out as the sun breaks through the gray clouds over Puget Sound.

He sets his coffee mug down on a side table beside a small leather journal.

PETER (V.O.)
The weight of thirty years was gone. I was free to live without fear, guilt, or judgment. Somewhere out there, she's happy. And so am I.

Peter smiles, looking out at the open water.

PETER
(whispering to himself)
President Peter Olson.

FADE OUT.
